	"filament_notes": [
		"colorFabb allPHA (pure PHA, 'alpha'). Source: official TDS v1.0 + colorFabb helpcenter. CRITICAL: COLD/UNHEATED bed - ALL plate temps 0. A heated plate induces crystallization = warping of bottom layers. 100% part cooling from layer 2 (layer 1 fan-off for cold-plate grip) to slow crystallization and set the model. P2S enclosed: BOTH doors OPEN + chamber heating OFF - remove glass front if possible; chamber must stay near ambient. PLATE: textured PEI (Bambu equivalent of colorFabb's favourite carborundum glass) + light coat of cold spray glue (release/sacrificial layer, same role as 3DLac or diluted wood glue). Do NOT use CryoGrip - aggressive cold grip + allPHA over-adhesion = unremovable part / plate damage. REMOVAL (official): big flat parts adhere HARD cold; heat plate to 90C, wait 15 min for bottom layers to heat through (heat crystallizes them and releases grip), then slide a thin sharp scraper underneath all around while still hot. Small parts / no brim release far easier. DRYING: NOT needed - allPHA is bacterial fat, barely hygroscopic. Temp 180-200C (195 mid for 0.6). Speed 30-60 mm/s (TDS) - do not exceed. Retraction a bit LOWER than PLA; gaps in outer walls = retract too high, reduce toward 0.5. Brim: colorFabb uses 20 perimeters for corner hold. Material is BRITTLE (4.5% strain at break, notched Charpy 3.4) - use gyroid infill + adequate walls for functional parts. HDT 153C. Flow 0.95 placeholder - run flow cal. Non-abrasive; hardened nozzle not required."
	],
